  "root_cause_scope": "The old age>=2 condition ignores work progress after a newly observed idle generation: units resets to zero, then age alone forces delay on the very first unit. Serial checkpoint sits after each submitted record. +5933 checkpoints/+5900 yields and +5932 submitted records show this path dominates output. The callback count also increased by 52887; these were real idle observations, not one uninterrupted stall.",
  "counter_limits": [
    "A vTaskDelay(1) counter is not measured blocked time: duration depends on tick phase and ready tasks.",
    "idleGeneration counts callback executions, including interrupt wakeups; not CPU percentage or elapsed ticks.",
    "Query windows differ from formal capture bounds and from each other.",
    "USB sink rejects, ordinary log line drops, driver submission and host missing frames are distinct counts.",
    "No MFAULT/ASCII CRC/identity failure does not mean all ADC points valid: X02 and X12 remain in the real capture.",
    "The older throughput run used a different selected SPI clock; do not attribute the complete acquisition FPS difference to this scheduling change."
  ],
  "change": {
    "graceUnits": 2,
    "idleBudgetTicks": 2,
    "backstopTicks": 4,
    "maxWorkUnits": 32,
    "credit_rule": "Only a real nonzero idle generation change renews grace. Own yield and notifications do not. Generation zero starts with grace exhausted.",
    "backstop_rule": "age>=4 ticks blocks once even on the first unit; age>=2 blocks after two units in the observed idle epoch. At most one delay(1) per checkpoint.",
    "preserved": [
      "No acquisition FPS cap",
      "No changed ADC timeout or spread threshold",
      "No watchdog disable or substitute feeding",
      "Control/lifecycle priorities and packet ownership unchanged",
      "Real DRAM idle observer and snapshot semantics unchanged"
    ]
  },
